# Persian locale for fa products

## Calendar

- User-facing dates are **Jalali (شمسی)**.
- DB stores Gregorian timezone-aware datetimes.
- Use `{% load persian %}{{ dt|jalali }}` or `apps.common.persian.format_jalali`.

## Money (shops)

- Default currency label: **تومان**.
- Always thousand-separate: `{{ price|toman }}` → `185,000 تومان`.
- Convert ×10 to ریال only at payment gateway calls.

## Numerals and bidi

- Persian digits are display only: `{{ price|toman|fa_digits }}`. Never store,
  post, or parse them — normalise input with `str.translate` first.
- Phones, codes and any Latin value inside Persian copy go in `<bdi>`
  (`<bdi dir="ltr">{{ phone }}</bdi>`).
- Persian spelling needs نیم‌فاصله (می‌شود، کتاب‌ها) and Persian punctuation
  (`،` `؟` «…» `٪`).

## UI (mandatory for fa screens)

- Follow skill **`persian-ui`**: complete RTL compositions, self-hosted
  Vazirmatn/Estedad, Persian chrome, no starter English, no Latin deco heroes.
- Self-host fonts and scripts — foreign CDNs are unreliable from Iran.
- The `[dir="rtl"]` layer in `tokens.css` / `base.css` handles tracking,
  leading, icon mirroring and input direction. Write logical CSS so it keeps
  working; details in `persian-ui/rtl-engineering.md`.
- Pair with `ui-ux` quality bar before calling a page done.

See skills: `persian-ui`, `persian-locale`, `persian-ecommerce`, `ui-ux`.
